nv-exp-index-range: TPMI_RH_NV_EXP_INDEX is the external NV Index range

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Part 2, Table "Definition of (TPM_HANDLE)
TPMI_RH_NV_EXP_INDEX Type"): "{EXTERNAL_NV_FIRST:EXTERNAL_NV_LAST} | range of
external NV Indexes", "#TPM_RC_VALUE | error returned if the handle is out of
range".

The reference's TPMI_RH_NV_EXP_INDEX_RANGES admit {NV_INDEX_FIRST:
NV_INDEX_LAST} instead, so the nvIndex of a TPMS_NV_PUBLIC_EXP_ATTR (the
TPM_HT_EXTERNAL_NV member of a TPM2B_NV_PUBLIC_2) accepts ordinary NV Index
handles and rejects every external NV handle with TPM_RC_VALUE (as the public
tcgtpm, ibmswtpm2 and tpm-rs do not).
diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/support/Marshal.c b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/support/Marshal.c
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/support/Marshal.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/support/Marshal.c
@@ -979,8 +979,11 @@ TPMI_RH_NV_LEGACY_INDEX_MarshalUnmarshal(
                                        ARRAYSIZE(TPMI_RH_NV_LEGACY_INDEX_RANGES));
 }
 
+// tpm-rs differential testing -- spec deviation fix (NOT determinism): Part 2,
+// TPMI_RH_NV_EXP_INDEX: "{EXTERNAL_NV_FIRST:EXTERNAL_NV_LAST} | range of external
+// NV Indexes"; upstream admits the ordinary NV Index range instead.
 const TPM_HANDLE_RANGE TPMI_RH_NV_EXP_INDEX_RANGES[] = {
-    {NV_INDEX_FIRST, NV_INDEX_LAST},
+    {EXTERNAL_NV_FIRST, EXTERNAL_NV_LAST},
 };
 
 // Table "Definition of TPMI_RH_NV_EXP_INDEX Type" (Part 2: Structures)
